     zzmmaazzee draws a first-person view of a walled maze and lets
     you walk it: walls stand full height around you, shown in
     perspective and dithered lighter the closer they are.  Find
     your way around; there is nothing to collect and no monster
     to meet - the walk itself is the game.  It must be run under
     the zzvviieeww desktop and accepts the standard window _o_p_t_i_o_n_s of
     GUI applications; see zzvviieeww.

     Movement is by keyboard, a step or a turn at a time; held
     keys repeat, which makes the motion continuous:

              ww, _u_p _a_r_r_o_w       walk forward
              ss, _d_o_w_n _a_r_r_o_w     walk backward
              aa, _l_e_f_t _a_r_r_o_w     turn left
              dd, _r_i_g_h_t _a_r_r_o_w    turn right
              FF1111               the help window (also the menu's Help entry)
              qq                 quit (also the menu's Quit entry)

     Each step is a quarter of a maze cell; each turn is a six-
     teenth of a full circle, so sixteen presses of dd face you
     back the way you came.  You cannot walk through walls: a
     blocked step slides along the wall instead, which helps in
     tight corners.

     A middle click on the window replays the current selection
     as keystrokes, one character per key.  Select a string of
     movement letters anywhere - or load one with hhrrcclliipp - and
     middle-click the maze to walk the recorded route.

