NNOOTTEESS
     Distance is shown by dither: near walls are light, far walls
     dark, and walls faced head-on are one shade lighter than
     walls seen along their length.  If the whole view turns a
     single even gray, you are standing with your nose against a
     wall - turn with aa or dd and the maze comes back.

     The window has a fixed size (the -SS option is ignored).  The
     rr key switches between the two renderers the program carries
     - wall projection from a BSP tree (the default) and column
     raycasting - which draw the same scene and differ only in
     speed; it exists for comparing the two and is not needed for
     play.
